pe="html">Fighting has returned to northern Ethiopia, shattering a fragile peace in the region. DW spoke to civilians caught in the crossfire amid communication blackouts, as rebel and federal forces keep battling for territory.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>TV journalist is crowned king of Uganda's Tooro Kingdom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4ba0691bd509f11f1e2d61dc0e1f4717ceb062a517686c41361ce69ca0fa2e6</id><updated>2026-09-30T15:00:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911--6e0b4c2080aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Edward Rukidi Kijanangoma has ascended to the throne after King Oyo died at the age of 34 due to a cancer battle. He previously worked for Ugandan broadcaster UBC as a TV anchor and editor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
